    "Scouting Notes": "Olson was a high school pick, taken in the 13th round of the 2018 draft, who has shown some serious development the last few seasons. \n\nOlson had bumped his velo from upper 80's touching 92-93, to now sitting at 93-94 and touching 95-97. The fastball appears to ride, making it a pitch he can get whiffs with at the top of the zone. He possesses multiple plus offspeed pitches, including a sharp slider and a power changeup in the mid upper 80's. His curveball has flashed plus, and is an above average pitch itself. \n\nThe issue that might pop up with Olson is his command. Which, is largely caused by a violent delivery with a lot of head movement. This has likely helped his uptick in velocity, but it will make it tougher to repeat his delivery and maintain command. This gives him a chance to end up a reliever. If he can improve the command, there's a very real chance that Olson is the best pitching prospect in the system in a year or two.",
